==Russian==

===Etymology===
'''Иван''', from Old Russian [[Иваннъ]], from Old Russian, Old Slavonic [[Иоаннъ]], from New Testament Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|Ἰωάννης |tr=Iōánnēs|lang=grc}}, from Hebrew {{term|יוֹחָנָן|lang=he|tr=[[Johanan|Jōħānān]]}}, perhaps from a former {{term|יְהוֹחָנָן|lang=he|tr=Yehochanan}} {{IPAchar|J<sup>ə</sup>hôħānān}}, meaning "God is gracious".

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-Иван.ogg|Audio}}

===Proper noun===
{{ru-proper noun|Иван|m}} (Iván)

# {{given name|male|lang=ru}}, [[Ivan]], equivalent to [[John]].
# [[India]] (''I'' in the [[Appendix:Russian phonetic alphabet|ICAO]] spelling alphabet)

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-anim-1||Ива́н}}

